      "widgets_values": [
        "For the target video, at 0.00 seconds into the target video, <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) is fully referenced.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] 3D CG, cinematic, the bioluminescent abyss shown in <Picture 1> continues, preserving the leviathan whale's position, the turquoise and violet neural light channels running the length of its body, the field of glowing cyan micro-plankton, and the dark indigo water. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed toward the whale's head as the light channels across its throat and ventral pleats brighten and dim in a steady pulse. Glass jellyfish drift through the foreground, their bells flashing pale cyan. Volumetric turquoise god-rays sweep down through the water. The whale's tail sweeps once and a pressure ring ripples outward through the plankton field. [Shot 2] At 00:08.000, the shot cuts to a tracking shot alongside the whale's flank, following the neural channels as they surge brighter toward the tail while the plankton streams past the lens.\n\noverall_soundscape: Deep resonant whale song calls across the distance and echoes back, layered over a muffled low-frequency underwater pressure rumble. Metallic sonar pings ring out at intervals and decay slowly. Faint crystalline chimes sound as the jellyfish drift past, and the water surges as the whale's tail sweeps.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A slow electronic score at about 80 BPM in a minor key, built on a deep sub-bass 808 that lands on every downbeat with silence between the hits. Wide analog synth pads sustain underneath while a sparse reverbed piano motif answers every second bar and low cello swells enter through the middle. The arrangement starts sparse, the bass enters near four seconds, and the instrumentation builds to its heaviest point at the end.",
        672,
        384,
        124
      ],
      "title": "fl2va - full music prompt"
    },
